msgstr "Límite superior"

#: R/texts.R
msgid "Upper bound 0.85 to 0.90: acceptable only for conceptually similar constructs"
msgstr ""
"Límite superior 0.85 a 0.90: aceptable solo para constructos conceptualmente "
"similares"

#: R/texts.R
msgid "Upper bound 0.90 or more: discriminant validity not established"
msgstr "Límite superior 0.90 o más: validez discriminante no establecida"

#: R/texts.R
msgid "Upper bound below 0.85: distinct constructs"
msgstr "Límite superior menor de 0.85: constructos distintos"

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"Upper bound: the one-sided 95%% bootstrap upper bound (the 95th percentile "
"of %d admissible resamples). Discriminant validity holds when it stays below "
"the threshold (Henseler et al., 2015, see references)."
msgstr ""
"Límite superior: el límite superior bootstrap unilateral al 95%% (el "
"percentil 95 de %d réplicas admisibles). Hay validez discriminante cuando "
"queda por debajo del umbral (Henseler et al., 2015, vea las referencias)."

#: R/texts.R
msgid "very weak"
msgstr "muy débil"

#: plssem/results/vif.columns.title
#: plssem/results/vifStruct.columns.title
msgid "VIF"
msgstr "VIF"

#: plssem/results/vif.columns.superTitle
#: plssem/results/vifStruct.columns.superTitle
msgid "VIF CI"
msgstr "IC del VIF"

#: R/texts.R
msgid "Warnings"
msgstr "Advertencias"

#: R/texts.R
msgid "weak"
msgstr "débil"

#: plssem/results/measurement.columns.title
msgid "Weight"
msgstr "Peso"

#: plssem/results/measurement.columns.superTitle
msgid "Weight CI"
msgstr "IC del peso"

#: R/texts.R
msgid "What to do now"
msgstr "Qué hacer ahora"

#: plssem/options/latentFill/white.title
#: plssem/options/manifestFill/white.title
msgid "White"
msgstr "Blanco"

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"With the bootstrap, %d of %d paths are significant at %s%%. Not significant "
"(interval includes 0): %s."
msgstr ""
"Con el bootstrap, %d de %d rutas son significativas al %s%%. No "
"significativas (el intervalo incluye el 0): %s."

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"With the bootstrap, all %d paths are significant at %s%%: their intervals "
"exclude 0."
msgstr ""
"Con el bootstrap, las %d rutas son significativas al %s%%: sus intervalos "
"excluyen el 0."

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"With the bootstrap, the upper bound of HTMT reaches 0.85 or more for %s: "
"discriminant validity is not established for these pairs, even if the "
"estimate is lower."
msgstr ""
"Con el bootstrap, el límite superior del HTMT alcanza 0.85 o más en %s: no "
"hay validez discriminante establecida para estos pares, aunque la estimación "
"sea menor."

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"With the bootstrap, the upper bound of HTMT stays below 0.85 for all %d "
"pairs: discriminant validity is established."
msgstr ""
"Con el bootstrap, el límite superior del HTMT queda por debajo de 0.85 en "
"los %d pares: la validez discriminante queda establecida."

#: plssem/results/reliability.columns.title
msgid "ρA"
msgstr "ρA"

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"ρA comes from a consistent PLS estimation of the same model (same weights): "
"it is the reliability that consistent PLS uses to correct for measurement "
"error (Dijkstra & Henseler, 2015, see references)."
msgstr ""
"ρA sale de una estimación PLS consistente del mismo modelo (mismos pesos): "
"es la fiabilidad que PLS consistente usa para corregir el error de medida "
"(Dijkstra y Henseler, 2015, vea las referencias)."

#: plssem/results/reliability.columns.title
msgid "ρC"
msgstr "ρC"

#: plssem/results/reliability.columns.superTitle
msgid "ρC CI"
msgstr "IC de ρC"

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"ρC is McDonald's ω computed with the loadings of the PLS model. With PLS "
"these are composite loadings, which are inflated, so ρC is an upper bound of "
"reliability; with consistent PLS they are common-factor loadings and ρC is "
"close to the ω of a factor analysis. The optional ω (CFA) column estimates a "
"one-factor confirmatory factor analysis of each construct, outside the PLS "
"model (McDonald, 1999, see references): it is the reference used in "
"psychometrics. Common misreading: reporting ρC from plain PLS as if it were "
"the ω of a factor analysis."
msgstr ""
"ρC es la ω de McDonald calculada con las cargas del modelo PLS. Con PLS son "
"cargas de compuestos, que están infladas, así que ρC es un límite superior "
"de la fiabilidad; con PLS consistente son cargas de factor común y ρC queda "
"cerca de la ω de un análisis factorial. La columna opcional ω (AFC) estima "
"un análisis factorial confirmatorio de un factor para cada constructo, fuera "
"del modelo PLS (McDonald, 1999, vea las referencias): es la referencia usada "
"en psicometría. Lectura errónea frecuente: informar la ρC de PLS simple como "
"si fuera la ω de un análisis factorial."

#: plssem/results/reliability.columns.title
msgid "ω (CFA)"
msgstr "ω (AFC)"
